WITHDRAWAL OF COUNSEL 
 
The proposed order granting an attorney’s motion to withdraw will include: 
 
 
This case will be stayed for thirty days to give the withdrawing attorney’s client time to 
retain new counsel. However, after thirty (30) days from the date of the order granting the 
withdrawal, the case will move forward whether the client retains new counsel or not; and the 
withdrawal without more will not be grounds for a continuance of the trial or final hearing. At 
that point, if the client does not have new counsel, the client will represent himself or herself pro 
se and be responsible to comply with all deadlines, procedures and law governing the case, just 
as an attorney would be, unless and until an attorney appears for the client. 
 
 
The withdrawing attorney will thoroughly explain the above stay provision to the client. 
If after using all means available, the attorney is unable to communicate with the client, the 
attorney will mail a copy of this order to the client’s most recent and accurate mail and email 
addresses known. 
